    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d881">

                <pb facs="0755" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg743"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51 Public Works Debt/290</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Beaulac</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2861</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-02-20">February 20, 1940</date>.<lb/>[Received February
                        21.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With further reference to the unpaid
                    portion of the public works debt, I have the honor to report that I discussed
                    the prospect of payment with the Secretary of State<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d881-f1"/> this morning.</p>
                <p>The Secretary said that he had had several conversations in the matter with the
                        President<anchor n="16" xml:id="d881-f2"/> and other officials of the
                    Government recently, and he thought that there would be no difficulty in the way
                    of congressional approval of the settlements already agreed upon. He said that,
                    in his opinion, it was a question of weeks, and possibly of days, now before
                    such congressional approval would be given. He promised to continue to pursue
                    the matter, and reiterated his previously expressed conviction that the prompt
                    payment of this debt would be in Cuba’s interest.</p>
                <p>I told Dr. Campa that, whereas I had had no conversations with General
                        Menocal<anchor n="17" xml:id="d881-f3"/> on the subject, it had been
                    reported to me by several persons that he had offered to cooperate in the matter
                    of congressional approval. The Secretary said that that was his understanding
                    also.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard L.
                    Beaulac</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
